<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia scraps bid for last three power plants.</title>
<headline>Colombia scraps bid for last three power plants.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Mines and Energy Ministry was forced to scrap the sell-off of the three remaining power plants in the first phase of its energy sector privatization after no bids were received.</p>
<p>The plants at Ocoa, Gualanday and Yumbo are currently run by the state oil company Ecopetrol. None of the nine foreign investors which had shown interest in three other plants submitted a bid, a ministry spokesman said.</p>
</text>
